# sixfiveohtwo stage 4 expectations.
# Stack ops (PHA/PLA/PHP/PLP), SP tracking, JSR/RTS nesting, JMP abs,
# JMP (ind) incl. the NMOS page-wrap bug.
#
# Marker order (= store order): $F001 after the PHA/PLA round trip,
# $F002 after the PLA-of-$00 zero pull (stx keeps the pulled flags
# intact), $F003 inside sub2 (deepest JSR level), $F004 inside sub1
# after the inner call returned, $F005 in the JMP (ind) stub (normal
# pointer), $F006 in the JMP (ind) stub (page-wrap pointer), $F000
# final marker (reached on the main flow via the jmp jsec navigation
# jump and the ind stubs' jumps back).
#
# JSR pushes return-1 (the address of its high operand byte; RTS adds
# 1 back). jsr sub1 sits at $0263, so the outer return-1 is $0265
# ($01FD=high $02, $01FC=low $65). jsr sub2 sits at $0283, so the
# inner return-1 is $0285 ($01FB=high $02, $01FA=low $85). R P is the
# PC when the marker store commits: the address of the instruction
# right after the 3-byte marker sta/stx.

M F001 C3

F N 1
F Z 0
F C 0
F V 0
F D 0
F I 1
R A C3
R X FD
R Y 00
R S FD
R P 0214

# --- PLA of $00: N=0, Z=1 (stx marker store does not touch flags) ---
M F002 FD

F N 0
F Z 1
F C 0
F V 0
F D 0
F I 1
R A 00
R X FD
R Y 00
R S FD
R P 0220

# --- inside sub2 (deepest level): SP=$F9 after two JSRs; both
# return-1 pairs on the stack; X=$F9 from sub2's TSX ---
M F003 D2

F N 1
F Z 0
F C 1
F V 0
F D 0
F I 1
R A D2
R X F9
R Y 00
R S F9
R P 029F

# outer return-1 ($0259) at $01FD/$01FC
C 01FD 02
C 01FC 65
# inner return-1 ($0285) at $01FB/$01FA
C 01FB 02
C 01FA 85

# --- inside sub1, after the inner call returned: SP restored to $FB,
# outer return-1 bytes intact below; X=$F9 left over from sub2 ---
M F004 D1

F N 1
F Z 0
F C 1
F V 0
F D 0
F I 1
R A D1
R X F9
R Y 00
R S FB
R P 0290

C 01FD 02
C 01FC 65

# --- JMP (ind) stub, normal zero-page pointer ($52/$53 -> $0300) ---
M F005 D5

F N 1
F Z 0
F C 1
F V 0
F D 0
F I 1
R A D5
R X FD
R Y 00
R S FD
R P 030A

# --- JMP (ind) stub, page-wrap pointer (low from $10FF, high from
# $1000 through the NMOS wrap -> $0500) ---
M F006 D4

F N 1
F Z 0
F C 1
F V 0
F D 0
F I 1
R A D4
R X FD
R Y 00
R S FD
R P 050A

# --- final marker: very last data write on the main flow. Preceded
# by ldx #$E7, ldy #$38, clv (V=0), sec (C=1), lda #$96 (N=1, Z=0).
# D and I are untouched reset values (SED/SEI/CLI never used). SP
# balanced back to $FD by the two RTS. ---

M F000 96

F N 1
F Z 0
F C 1
F V 0
F D 0
F I 1
R A 96
R X E7
R Y 38
R S FD
R P 0613

# --- PHA/PLA round trips and SP tracking via TSX ---
C F100 FC
C F101 C3
C F102 FD
C F103 00

# --- PHP->PLA exact P bytes (B=1, bit5=1; second with N=1, C=1) ---
C F104 34
C F105 B5

# --- PLP restores: C (adc #$00 probe $41) and Z ($60 guard) ---
C F106 41
C F107 60

# --- JSR/RTS: SP inside sub1/sub2, sub2's store, sub1's store after
# the inner call returned, SP after both RTS ---
C F108 FB
C F109 7E
C F10A 3C
C F10B FD
C F10F F9

# --- JMP abs skipped the poison; both ind jumps landed ---
C F10C 11
C F10D 33
C F10E 55

# --- fail/poison markers must NOT have been stored ---
C F140 00
C F141 00
C F142 00
C F143 00
C F144 00
C F145 00
C F146 00
C F147 00

# --- stack bytes persist after both RTS (pulls never clear) ---
C 01FD 02
C 01FC 65
C 01FB 02
C 01FA 85

# --- pointer setup scratch (zero page and wrap pointer pages) ---
C 52 00
C 53 03
C 54 04
C 10FF 00
C 1000 05
C 1100 06